---
/**
 * "/" — THE NEW BUILD'S HOME (release restructure, Oscar 2026-08-10).
 * This file is the former landing.astro moved onto the root route;
 * /landing is now a redirect stub to here. The holding face that
 * previously occupied "/" was a thin duplicate of /holding-3, which
 * remains untouched — no archive copy needed.
 *
 * A fresh page: it shares the visual system with the archived build
 * (ground, grain, top nav, Lenis/GSAP scroll architecture) but not its
 * files — everything is scoped to the `landing-v2` body class and lives
 * under src/{components,styles,scripts}/landing/. Nothing here touches
 * /old, /services or the holding routes.
 *
 * R49 (Oscar, 2026-09-04) — THIS FILE IS NOW THE ROUTE, NOT THE PAGE.
 * Every section, every boot call and the whole scroll architecture moved
 * VERBATIM into components/landing/LandingBody.astro, so that
 * /landing-splash-b can render the IDENTICAL page with a different
 * splash without forking a line of it. The two routes therefore cannot
 * drift: the only difference between them is LandingBody's `splash`
 * prop. R75: that prop is now flag-driven — the shipped splash by
 * default, the alternate one on staging.
 * Verified: this route's built markup is unchanged by the extraction.
 *
 * STAGING ONLY. The root serves the holding page; this route is not
 * promoted anywhere until Oscar says so. See docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md.
 */
import LandingBody from '../components/landing/LandingBody.astro';
import { SPLASH_B_ON_ROOT } from '../data/flags.js';
---

{/* R75 (Oscar, 2026-09-05): which splash the home page boots. The flag is
    OFF by default — including in dev and in any production build — so
    this renders the shipped splash exactly as before, and staging alone
    serves the alternate one (stage.sh passes it per deployment). The page
    itself is identical either way; only the splash component differs. */}
<LandingBody splash={SPLASH_B_ON_ROOT ? 'b' : 'a'} />
